.TH TUI_TREE_INIT 3 2026-10-20 "libtuikit 0.10" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_tree_init, tui_tree_free, tui_tree_set_rows, tui_tree_row_at,
tui_tree_selected_row, tui_tree_is_open, tui_tree_set_open,
tui_tree_open_all, tui_tree_close_all, tui_tree_select_row,
tui_tree_show_matches, tui_tree_show_counts, tui_tree_marker,
tui_tree_handle, tui_tree_render \- a list whose rows open and close
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/tree.h>
.PP
.B typedef struct tui_treerow {
.B "    const char *id;  int depth;  int children;"
.B } tui_treerow;
.PP
.BI "void tui_tree_init(tui_tree *" t );
.BI "void tui_tree_free(tui_tree *" t );
.BI "int  tui_tree_set_rows(tui_tree *" t ", const tui_treerow *" rows ", int " n );
.BI "int  tui_tree_row_at(const tui_tree *" t ", int " item );
.BI "int  tui_tree_selected_row(const tui_tree *" t );
.BI "int  tui_tree_is_open(const tui_tree *" t ", int " row );
.BI "int  tui_tree_set_open(tui_tree *" t ", int " row ", int " open );
.BI "int  tui_tree_open_all(tui_tree *" t );
.BI "void tui_tree_close_all(tui_tree *" t );
.BI "int  tui_tree_select_row(tui_tree *" t ", int " row );
.BI "int  tui_tree_show_matches(tui_tree *" t ", const unsigned char *" match );
.BI "void tui_tree_show_counts(tui_tree *" t ", int " on );
.BI "const char *tui_tree_marker(const tui_tree *" t ", int " row );
.BI "int  tui_tree_handle(tui_tree *" t ", const tui_event *" ev );
.PP
.BI "typedef int (*tui_tree_draw_fn)(void *" ctx ", tui_canvas " label ", int " row ,
.BI "                                int " selected ", tui_style " base );
.BI "void tui_tree_render(tui_tree *" t ", tui_canvas " c ", tui_style " blank ,
.BI "                     tui_style " selected ", tui_tree_draw_fn " draw ", void *" ctx );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The tree of the interface policy (policies/tui-interface-model.md, "Trees"),
over
.BR tui_listview (3):
every program's tree looks and behaves the same.
The program gives its rows in pre-order, each with an identity string, its
depth (0 on the top level, at most one more than the row above) and its number
of children.
The widget keeps which branches are open, keyed by the identity, and the
list view (the
.I list
member) holds the visible rows only.
.PP
Every branch is closed on opening.
The first two cells of a row are the marker, returned by
.BR tui_tree_marker ():
"+ " for a closed row with children, "\- " for an open one, two blanks for a
leaf.
.PP
.BR tui_tree_set_rows ()
is a load or a reload.
The open state and the selection are kept by identity (a selected row that is
gone leaves the selection at the same position, clamped).
The previous rows must still be valid during the call, the new ones until the
next.
It returns \-1 and leaves the tree unchanged for a missing id, a depth below 0
or more than one deeper than the row above (errno EINVAL), or without memory.
.BR tui_tree_row_at ()
maps a list item to its row,
.BR tui_tree_selected_row ()
gives the selected row.
.BR tui_tree_set_open ()
opens or closes one row and keeps the selection on it;
.BR tui_tree_open_all ()
and
.BR tui_tree_close_all ()
are for the program's ':' menu (no letter is taken for them); after a close
the selection moves to its nearest visible ancestor.
.BR tui_tree_select_row ()
opens the branches above a row and selects it.
.PP
.BR tui_tree_show_matches ()
shows a filter or a search: the array has one byte per row, non-zero for a
match, and the branches above every match are opened.
What was open before is remembered; calling it with NULL clears the filter and
restores that state.
A new call replaces the earlier match; after a reload while filtering, call it
again.
.PP
.BR tui_tree_handle ()
applies the keys of the policy and returns 1 for them:
Right and
.B l
open the row at the cursor (on an open row they move to its first child);
Left and
.B h
close it (on a closed row or a leaf they move to its parent);
Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End, their letters
.BR j ", " k ", " ctrl\-f ", " ctrl\-b ", " g ", " G
move over the visible rows only.
Enter is not the widget's (it stays "open the row" of the program), and
returns 0.
.PP
.BR tui_tree_render ()
draws the visible rows: the marker at the first two cells, two cells of indent
per level, then the label, drawn by
.I draw
into a canvas already cleared with the row's style, which it returns as
.IR base .
The row's style is
.I selected
on the selected row, else
.IR blank .
With
.BR tui_tree_show_counts (t,\ 1)
a closed row with children shows " (N)" after the label, N being its number of
children.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
static int draw_label(void *ctx, tui_canvas c, int row, int sel, tui_style st) {
    const char *const *names = ctx;
    tui_canvas_put(c, 0, 0, names[row], st);
    return (int)strlen(names[row]);
}
\&...
tui_tree_set_rows(&tree, rows, n);
tui_tree_render(&tree, pane, TUI_STYLE_DEFAULT, TUI_STYLE_SELECTION,
                draw_label, names);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
